1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:07,384
These are the browser tests for Synaps Optic. Each one opens
a page in Chrome and checks it the way a person would.

2
00:00:08,034 --> 00:00:15,323
In the editor, each button on the left rail opens its own
panel, and only one button is highlighted at a time.

3
00:00:15,973 --> 00:00:23,169
The Videos panel has three tabs: edit, effects and
transitions. Exactly one is selected after each click.

4
00:00:23,819 --> 00:00:29,320
The select and hand tools work like a switch. Choosing one
turns the other off.

5
00:00:29,970 --> 00:00:33,916
The inspector on the left can be collapsed to give the
preview more room.

6
00:00:34,566 --> 00:00:41,170
The timeline shows all three clips. The two scenes are video
clips, and the voice-over is an audio clip.

7
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:52,314
Next, every page loads with the Synapspaces design system:
the Geist font, a white page, and nothing spilling off the
side. This is the projects page.

8
00:00:52,964 --> 00:00:54,518
Now the editor.

9
00:00:55,168 --> 00:00:58,814
Now the Recast page.

10
00:00:59,464 --> 00:01:02,002
Now the take review page.

11
00:01:02,652 --> 00:01:04,763
Now the references page.

12
00:01:05,413 --> 00:01:07,640
Now the invites page.

13
00:01:08,290 --> 00:01:11,486
Now the sign-in page.

14
00:01:12,136 --> 00:01:18,961
Each page's top bar shows the Synapspaces logo and the light
and dark switch. This is the projects page.

15
00:01:19,611 --> 00:01:23,163
And the Recast page.

16
00:01:23,813 --> 00:01:25,808
And the take review page.

17
00:01:26,458 --> 00:01:28,838
And the references page.

18
00:01:29,488 --> 00:01:31,444
And the invites page.

19
00:01:32,094 --> 00:01:36,086
And the sign-in page.

20
00:01:36,736 --> 00:01:41,877
The navigation moves between Projects and Recast, and the
logo leads back home.

21
00:01:42,527 --> 00:01:45,962
Clicking a project card opens that project in the editor.

22
00:01:46,612 --> 00:01:55,399
On the sign-in page, buttons are rounded pills, fields are
the standard height, and placeholder text uses the design
system's grey.

23
00:01:56,049 --> 00:02:02,223
The AI prompt on the home page accepts a description, and
the aspect ratio can be changed.

24
00:02:02,873 --> 00:02:10,081
On the take review page, the compare view loads frames from
the source clip and the cat take, side by side.

25
00:02:10,731 --> 00:02:16,418
All five shot tabs fit in their row. This test caught the
last tab being cut off.

26
00:02:17,068 --> 00:02:22,128
Selecting a shot opens its review panel and moves the frame
slider to that shot.

27
00:02:22,778 --> 00:02:30,462
The compare view switches between side by side and a wipe.
The slider moves the wipe, and the W key switches back.

28
00:02:31,112 --> 00:02:36,962
The arrow keys step one frame at a time. With shift held,
they jump five frames.

29
00:02:37,612 --> 00:02:43,101
If the backend cannot be reached, the loading screen still
goes away instead of getting stuck.

30
00:02:43,751 --> 00:02:48,347
Dark mode. With the computer set to light, the editor is
light.

31
00:02:48,997 --> 00:02:55,044
With the computer set to dark, the editor turns dark, and
the main buttons flip to light.

32
00:02:55,694 --> 00:03:01,892
The switch in the top bar changes the theme. The choice is
remembered after a reload and carries into the editor.

33
00:03:02,542 --> 00:03:08,068
The saved theme is applied before the page appears, so there
is no white flash.

34
00:03:08,718 --> 00:03:13,848
Video and images keep their black background in both themes.
This is the editor.

35
00:03:14,498 --> 00:03:16,864
And again on the take review page.

36
00:03:17,514 --> 00:03:19,834
And again on the take review page.

37
00:03:20,484 --> 00:03:24,441
Finally, the switch in the editor's own top bar works too.

38
00:03:25,091 --> 00:03:30,999
36 tests passed. The tests run automatically on every push
to the repository.

